# Auto-log app edits to Slack

Whenever an agent makes code or content changes to this app (the Infinity
Windows app in this repo), it must post a short, plain-English summary to the
Slack channel **#infinity-app-changelog** so non-technical stakeholders always
have a running record of what changed.

## Channel

- Channel name: `#infinity-app-changelog`
- Channel ID: `C0BJ349BJNR`
- Post via the Slack MCP tool `slack_send_message` (already authenticated).

## When to post

Post **once per task**, right after the work is done and just before you finish
your turn — specifically:

- After you open the PR (per the ship-via-PR rule), include the PR URL.
- If the change is explicitly "local only" / "don't PR", still post the summary
  and note that it was not shipped.
- Do **not** post for read-only work (questions, exploration, reviews) where no
  files were changed.
- Post only **one** summary per task, not one per file or per commit.

## Message format

Keep it short and readable for non-technical people (Taylor & Ammon). Use this
shape:

```
:hammer_and_wrench: *<short title of the change>*
<1-3 plain-English bullet points on what changed and why it matters to users>
PR: <url, or "local only — not shipped">
```

Guidelines:
- Plain English, no jargon or file dumps. Describe user-visible impact first.
- Skip internal noise (lockfile bumps, formatting-only churn) unless that was
  the whole point of the task.
- Never include secrets, tokens, or credentials in the message.
- If the Slack post fails, do not block the task — mention the failure in your
  final chat summary so it can be retried.
